Helpers: libgcc.a of gcc-14 (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0, SHA-256
60dbf748e1c310aa50300a33f30bf4ee070061071aee74a52cf115a7b8765e50.

Command, for CC in gcc-14 and clang-19, LEVEL in -O0 and -O2, KIND in 32, 64
and 128, FORM in 1 (the helper through a pointer) and 0 (the operators), and
SELECT empty (the grid) or -DSAMPLE (the 50 sample operand sets):
  CC -std=gnu11 LEVEL -frounding-math -ffp-contract=off -DKIND=KIND
     -DFORM=FORM -DMODES=4 SELECT floating-complex-grid.c -o grid -lm && ./grid

All 48 executions print the same four lines for each KIND and selection.
Each record is K=KIND for the grid or S=KIND for the sample, the rounding
mode (0 nearest, 1 upward, 2 downward, 3 toward zero), then the bits hash
and the flags hash of the products and of the quotients. The machine-read
lines follow the marker.

